# Creates tomorrow's RunDate and loads jobs_dir into it (see spec 0009).
# --date T+1 is resolved relative to BORG_RUN_DATE (this job's own RunDate,
# injected by the agent), not wall-clock today, so a late or catch-up run
# still preloads the right day.
#
# No EnvVar here: BORG_COOKIE for this Command's own `borg` CLI call must come from the agent's
# own process environment (bin/agent.sh's own comment: it exports BORG_COOKIE "so a dispatched
# admin job's Command can invoke the borg CLI"). A hardcoded `EnvVar: BORG_COOKIE=borg` here used
# to override that inheritance with the literal string "borg" — harmless only by coincidence for
# an installation whose real cookie happens to also be "borg" (borg's own shared dev default);
# for any installation with its own distinct cookie, every dispatch of this job failed with
# "Cannot reach borg node" (observed directly, isolated by diagnostic logging showing BORG_COOKIE
# in the spawned command's actual environment as "borg" instead of the real one).
Master: any
Command: borg admin load-rundate --date T+1
Host: any
Days: d
StartAfter: 09:00
Timeout: 300
RepeatCount: 3
